      "side": 1,
      "message": "looks like we should disable the power path here, but we have to be careful not to do it in the dead battery case.\n\nperhaps we need a static variable to keep track of if we have ever toggled enable to on (and thus enabled the power path).\n\nstatic inline void pd_set_host_mode(int port, int enable)\n{\n\tstatic int has_been_enabled;\n\n\tif (enable) {\n\t\thas_been_enabled \u003d 1;\n\t\t/* we should be able to provide VBUS to USB device */\n\t\tboard_vbus_power_path(1);\n\t\t...\n\t} else {\n\t\t/*\n\t\t * disable power path if we have enabled host mode\n\t\t * to avoid dead battery case\n\t\t */\n\t\tif (has_been_enabled)\n\t\t\tboard_vbus_power_path(0);\n\t\t/* Kill VBUS power supply */\n\t\tcharger_enable_otg_power(0);\n\t\t...\n\t}\n}\n\ni think this behavior matches what we have done on other boards.",
      "revId": "a53348ba814f1cb4d6054e666d2a5ff71256fda1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
